error[E0277]: `Vec<u8>` is not `Orderable`: it has no order target of its own
  --> tests/ui/negative_space/bytes_have_no_target_of_their_own.rs:14:34
   |
14 |     let _ = clear::Clear.encrypt(vec![1u8]);
   |                          ------- ^^^^^^^^^ has no order target of its own
   |                          |
   |                          required by a bound introduced by this call
   |
   = help: the trait `Orderable` is not implemented for `Vec<u8>`
   = note: name the target: `scheme.target(I64).encrypt_checked(value)`
   = note: there is no 8-bit target: an order term over 256 values reveals them, so an `i8` goes into `I16` or wider by name (`scheme.target(I16).encrypt(value)`), or into an equality index
   = note: bytes order only into a target named for them, `scheme.target(Bytes)`: no ordering operator compares bytes
   = help: the following other types implement trait `Orderable`:
             &String
             &chrono::datetime::DateTime<chrono::offset::utc::Utc>
             &chrono::naive::date::NaiveDate
             &f32
             &f64
             &i128
             &i16
             &i32
           and $N others
note: required by a bound in `encrypt`
  --> src/scheme.rs
   |
   |     fn encrypt<V>(&self, value: V) -> Result<OrderTerm<Self::Term, V::Target>, Self::Error>
   |        ------- required by a bound in this associated function
   |     where
   |         V: Orderable + FitsIn<V::Target>,
   |            ^^^^^^^^^ required by this bound in `OrderEncrypt::encrypt`

